   "definition": "The occupant gas path starts at IP-UP, where it receives the entire anode gas from the single common mixing point (Xe during ignition, transition and time-limited fallback; N2 or N2/O2 in atmospheric operation), and ends at IP-DN, where it hands the gas (and in a source arm the pre-ionized flow) to the H-1 gas distributor at HALL_INLET_Z0. The occupant wall between IP-UP and IP-DN is the pressure boundary between the anode gas path and the chamber vacuum. The cathode gas never enters any occupant. This is the A5 reserved-interface location 'between feed/plenum and Hall ionization region'.",
