   "definition": "Electrical reference and emission containment of every occupant. The occupant body potential (and that of any interstage electrode) is declared once for all occupants and presented identically at IP-DN; the thruster floats, with the discharge supply between anode and cathode common; the occupant is separated from the common feed line by the common gas isolator upstream of IP-UP; source-drive returns (RF or microwave) are separated from the discharge return; emissions into common diagnostics are bounded by the dummy-load pickup control.",
