   "id": "PMI-10",
   "boundary": "allowable pressure drop",
   "definition": "Delta_p_occupant is the static-pressure rise that an occupant adds on the feed side at a given anode flow and gas. It is observed as the cold-flow manifold pressure (the common capacitance manometer upstream of IP-UP) at each W1 grid flow with that occupant installed. Everything downstream of IP-DN is H-1 and identical, so a difference in manifold pressure between occupants at identical flow and gas is a difference in occupant flow resistance. The allowable pressure drop is a common class: every occupant's cold-flow manifold pressure lies in one band around the PIM-0 value at every W1 test-point flow.",
   "requirements": [
    {
     "id": "PMI-10.R1",
     "text": "The manifold pressure at each grid flow is measured cold in every configuration in S1a and reported; the difference is part of R_install and is never corrected.",
